<title>GERMANY: UPS PLAYS DOWN COLOGNE AIRPORT PROTEST.</title>
<headline>UPS PLAYS DOWN COLOGNE AIRPORT PROTEST.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service of America Inc (UPS) has played down an employees' demonstration at Cologne airport on Tuesday night as simple leaflet distribution and little more.</p>
<p>&quot;There was no action apart from staff taking the leaflets. It did not have any positive reaction,&quot; a UPS Germany spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>A strike by the company's U.S. Teamster employees over concerns about wages, benefits, profit sharing, the creation of more full-time job opportunities and a limit to sub-contracting, has entered its 10th day.</p>
<p>&quot;Neither side is interested in escalating the situation here because the situation in Germany is completely different to the U.S.,&quot; the UPS Germany spokesman added.</p>
